again</guid><category>Men's Basketball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Miles Sadler has been named Big 12 Freshman of the Week and to the Big 12 Starting 5" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/23/MBB26_Big12WeeklyAward_1920x1080_Sadler2.png" /><br /><br />IRVING, Texas - Houston's Dedan Thomas Jr. took home Player of the Week honors after guiding the Cougars to the Players Era 8 championship while West Virginia's Miles Sadler earned Freshman of the Week recognition for his performance at the same tournament in this week's Monster Energy Big 12 Men's Basketball weekly awards.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/23/MBB26_Big12WeeklyAward_1920x1080_Sadler2.png" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/23/MBB26_Big12WeeklyAward_1920x1080_Sadler2.png"><media:title>Miles Sadler has been named Big 12 Freshman of the Week and to the Big 12 Starting 5</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/23/MBB26_Big12WeeklyAward_1920x1080_Sadler2.png" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 14:52:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>4</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59751</s:story_id></item><item><title>Vanadia, Watters to Compete at NWCA All-Star Classic</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/23/wrestling-vanadia-watters-to-compete-at-nwca-all-star-classic</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/23/wrestling-vanadia-watters-to-compete-at-nwca-all-star-classic</guid><category>Wrestling</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="The Hope Coliseum floor setup for a WVU wrestling match on Nov. 22, 2026." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/22/Wrestling_vAmerican_11222026-9.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – Redshirt sophomore No. 13 Max Vanadia and redshirt junior No. 6 Ty Watters will represent the No. 23 West Virginia University wrestling team at the 2026 National Wrestling Coaches Association (NWCA) All-Star Classic at Rec Hall on the campus of Penn State University in University Park, Pennsylvania, on Nov. 24.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/22/Wrestling_vAmerican_11222026-9.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/22/Wrestling_vAmerican_11222026-9.jpg"><media:title>The Hope Coliseum floor setup for a WVU wrestling match on Nov. 22, 2026.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/22/Wrestling_vAmerican_11222026-9.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 13:38:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>18</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59750</s:story_id></item><item><title>Cross Country Team Named Student-Athletes of the Week</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/23/cross-country-team-named-student-athletes-of-the-week</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/23/cross-country-team-named-student-athletes-of-the-week</guid><category>Cross Country</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Cross Country team celebrates on the podium after finishing runner-up at the NCAA Championships" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/23/crosscountry.png" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The West Virginia University Cross Country team has been named the WVU Student-Athletes of the Week, presented by University Apartments.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/23/crosscountry.png" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/23/crosscountry.png"><media:title>Cross Country team celebrates on the podium after finishing runner-up at the NCAA Championships</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/23/crosscountry.png" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 11:42:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>10</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59749</s:story_id></item><item><title>West Virginia Heads to the Bahamas for the Battle 4 Atlantis</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/23/womens-basketball-west-virginia-heads-to-the-bahamas-for-the-battle-4-atlantis</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/23/womens-basketball-west-virginia-heads-to-the-bahamas-for-the-battle-4-atlantis</guid><category>Women's Basketball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Khy Ngodu matchup for the battle 4 atlantis" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/23/WBB26_MATCHUP_vsFLORIDA_1920x1080.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The No. 20-ranked West Virginia University women's basketball team heads to Paradise Island, The Bahamas, for two games at the Battle 4 Atlantis. The event runs from Nov. 24-26 with the Mountaineers playing on both Tuesday, against Florida, and Thursday, against Notre Dame, inside Imperial Hall.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/23/WBB26_MATCHUP_vsFLORIDA_1920x1080.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/23/WBB26_MATCHUP_vsFLORIDA_1920x1080.jpg"><media:title>Khy Ngodu matchup for the battle 4 atlantis</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/23/WBB26_MATCHUP_vsFLORIDA_1920x1080.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 10:00:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>9</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59748</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Fall in Double Overtime to Washington in NCAA Second Round</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/22/mens-soccer-mountaineers-fall-in-double-overtime-to-washington-in-ncaa-second-round</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/22/mens-soccer-mountaineers-fall-in-double-overtime-to-washington-in-ncaa-second-round</guid><category>Men's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Men's Soccer Huddle pregame against Washington" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/22/MSOC_WVUvsWashington_Nov22_2026_TT-1.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The No. 4-seed West Virginia University men's soccer team fell to No. 5-seed Washington, 1-0, in double-overtime, Sunday afternoon at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium. The Mountaineers end their season with a record of 13-3-4 while the Huskies improve to 12-4-5 and advance to the third round to play No. 1-seed Indiana.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/22/MSOC_WVUvsWashington_Nov22_2026_TT-1.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/22/MSOC_WVUvsWashington_Nov22_2026_TT-1.jpg"><media:title>Men's Soccer Huddle pregame against Washington</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/22/MSOC_WVUvsWashington_Nov22_2026_TT-1.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:32:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>6</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59747</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Fall at Kansas State in Four Sets</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/22/volleyball-mountaineers-fall-at-kansas-state-in-four-sets</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/22/volleyball-mountaineers-fall-at-kansas-state-in-four-sets</guid><category>Volleyball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="West Virginia volleyball huddles after a point while playing against Kansas State" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/22/DTB04257.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. - The West Virginia University volleyball team (13-13, 6-10 Big 12) dropped a four-set match to Kansas State on Sunday afternoon at Morgan Family Arena in Manhattan, Kansas. The Mountaineers fell by set scores of 25-21, 21-25, 30-28 and 25-18.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/22/DTB04257.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/22/DTB04257.jpg"><media:title>West Virginia volleyball huddles after a point while playing against Kansas State</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/22/DTB04257.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:40:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>17</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59746</s:story_id></item><item><title>No. 23 West Virginia Defeats American</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/22/wrestling-no-23-west-virginia-defeats-american</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/22/wrestling-no-23-west-virginia-defeats-american</guid><category>Wrestling</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Luke Satriano competes against a wrestler for American at Hope Coliseum on Nov. 22, 2026." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/22/Wrestling_vAmerican_11222026-2nd-2.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The No. 23 West Virginia University wrestling team defeated American, 28-6, at Hope Coliseum in Morgantown on Sunday.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/22/Wrestling_vAmerican_11222026-2nd-2.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/22/Wrestling_vAmerican_11222026-2nd-2.jpg"><media:title>Luke Satriano competes against a wrestler for American at Hope Coliseum on Nov. 22, 2026.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/22/Wrestling_vAmerican_11222026-2nd-2.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 15:32:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>18</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59745</s:story_id></item><item><title>West Tower Construction At Milan Puskar Stadium Will Halt Vehicular and Pedestrian Traffic</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/22/general-west-tower-construction-at-milan-puskar-stadium-will-halt-vehicular-and-pedestrian-traffic</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/22/general-west-tower-construction-at-milan-puskar-stadium-will-halt-vehicular-and-pedestrian-traffic</guid><category>Football, General</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Construction of the new West Tower at Milan Puskar Stadium will impact traffic and walking areas for the next two years." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/22/Stadium_Map__11-20_-transparent.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – With the completion of the 2026 home football schedule, demolition of the 46-year old press box at Milan Puskar Stadium will commence on Monday, Nov. 23.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/22/Stadium_Map__11-20_-transparent.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/22/Stadium_Map__11-20_-transparent.jpg"><media:title>Construction of the new West Tower at Milan Puskar Stadium will impact traffic and walking areas for the next two years.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/22/Stadium_Map__11-20_-transparent.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 11:00:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>3</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59744</s:story_id></item><item><title>Houston Kicks Late Field Goal to Down West Virginia</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/21/football-houston-kicks-late-field-goal-to-down-west-virginia</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/21/football-houston-kicks-late-field-goal-to-down-west-virginia</guid><category>Football</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="John Neider secures a 3-yard Michael Hawkins Jr. pass for a touchdown in the first quarter of West Virginia's game against 20th-ranked Houston at Milan Puskar Stadium." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/21/Neider-Main.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – Jonathan Dimas' 23-yard field goal with four seconds left lifted 20th-ranked Houston to a 34-31 victory over West Virginia today at Milan Puskar Stadium.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/21/Neider-Main.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/21/Neider-Main.jpg"><media:title>John Neider secures a 3-yard Michael Hawkins Jr. pass for a touchdown in the first quarter of West Virginia's game against 20th-ranked Houston at Milan Puskar Stadium.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/21/Neider-Main.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 17:34:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>2</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59743</s:story_id></item></channel></rss>